On Tue, Nov 2, 2010 at 11:03 AM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com> wrote:
> ...Gah, random gripe: give {su'u} some love!

I don't know how "su'u" works. The example in CLL is:

    ko zgana le su'u le ci smacu cu bajra
    "See how the three mice run!"

So "su'u" is being used for "nu tai ma kau".

The other gloss "you [imperative] observe the abstract-nature-of the
three mice running" makes little sense to me since I don't think
there's anything very abstract about three mice running.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

